 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T08:45+08:00",
 "answer": "Whether you can go jogging depends on your sensitivity and exact location on the island, as air quality currently ranges from **moderate to unhealthy** depending on the specific neighborhood. \n\n* **The General Situation:** Air quality readings across parts of Penang (such as George Town, Perai, and Bayan Lepas) are fluctuating. Some areas are registering moderate levels (acceptable for most, though sensitive individuals might feel mild irritation), while other hyper-local monitors show higher spikes in PM2.5 that cross into unhealthy territory for outdoor exercise.\n* **Health Recommendation:** If you are generally healthy, a light or moderate jog is usually okay if you stick to periods when the air feels clearer, but heavy or prolonged exertion might cause throat irritation or coughing if you hit a pocket of poor air. If you have asthma, allergies, or other respiratory sensitivities, it is safer to skip the outdoor run or head indoors.\n\n**Quick tip:** Before heading out, check a real-time tracking app (like IQAir, AccuWeather, or Malaysia's APIMS system) for your specific neighborhood, as air pollution can vary quite a bit between the coast, the hills, and urban areas.",
